# Target C-II — paired-remainder bathtub excludes the full-core branch through `t<=1.84370`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only full-core Type-II strengthening  
**Scope:** full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II branch  
**Dependencies:** scope-safe `g=0.007707` residual stability; hostile-audited two-leaf outer-energy architecture; repaired strong center/leaf branch; paired-remainder bathtub lemma  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_remainder_bathtub_exclusion_t184370.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The hostile-audited two-leaf argument currently excludes

\[
t={q-k\over D}\le1.84365.
\]

Its leaf energy ledger uses the paired terminal energy of the good O--O populations but discards the remaining retained outer occurrences in those same two leaf phases. The paired-remainder bathtub lemma shows that this discarded measure pays an additional one-well cost in each leaf.

Keeping that energy extends the same full-core exclusion to

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}\ge1.84370.
}
\tag{E70.1}
\]

The exact rounded package is

\[
h<0.00065,
\qquad
W<1.912984,
\qquad
E_{dom}>0.90689955,
\tag{E70.2}
\]

\[
z>2.21904,
\qquad
z_C,z_U,z_V>0.6904,
\tag{E70.3}
\]

\[
U,V<0.5436.
\tag{E70.4}
\]

Thus each leaf has retained O--O pair weight above `0.1468D`. After removing all pair weight with center degree at most half, each leaf still has more than `0.1076D` good pair weight. Trimming both good families to that common weight leaves at least `0.4752D` retained occurrence mass in each leaf outside the paired terminal submeasure. Those two remainders pay independent bathtub costs.

The resulting exact outer-energy contradiction has margin above

\[
8.0\times10^{-4}D.
\]

---

## 1. Residual stability remains in scope

Put

\[
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\qquad
C_{707}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.007707,
\]

and use

\[
x={\kappa\over2},
\qquad
h=U_{net}-C_{707},
\qquad
c=1.05.
\]

Then

\[
2\delta+x+h
=R_t:={9t\over2}-2\pi-C_{707}.
\tag{E70.5}
\]

The residual-stability theorem requires `U_net<=2.013`. The already-proved `t<=1.844` phase theorem gives total retained dominant outer mass above `1.848D`, hence

\[
\delta\ge F(1.848)-o(1),
\qquad
F(s)=s-6\sin(s/6).
\]

The exact verifier gives `F(1.848)>0.029`, so at `t<=1.84370`,

\[
U_{net}<1.957<2.013.
\]

Thus the audited residual estimate applies:

\[
R:=U_{net}-W\le1.05h,
\tag{E70.6}
\]

where `W=C+U+V` is the dominant exact `pi/3` orbit mass.

